#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059416 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69e91ce7-259a-5a11-bb79-7e6ad7ea86d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "4cd24c10-1838-5f4b-ac88-cfbfc2ec4c21" :question/math-academy-id "e-3518" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x - 30^{\\circ} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u\\cos v - \\cos u\\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and\n\n$$\nv=30^{\\circ}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (x - 30^{∘}) &= \\sin x\\cos 30^{∘} - \\cos x\\sin 30^{∘} \\\\\n&= \\sin x \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) - \\cos x \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x}{2} - \\frac{\\cos x}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x - \\cos x}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059417 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "7341638b-3c0f-5c10-8b7d-a2c313607bed" :question/math-academy-id "e-3519" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$.*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y) = \\sin x\\cos y - \\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\sin (\\frac{π}{3} - \\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{3})\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}) - \\cos (\\frac{π}{3})\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b12a7b7-1df3-5203-934e-8820604de3de" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "0ce71d86-7470-5d53-ac94-20b473889dee" :question/math-academy-id "e-9983" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v) = \\sin{u}\\cos{v} + \\cos{u}\\sin{v}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u = x$ and\n\n$$\nv = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (x + \\frac{π}{6}) &= \\sin x\\cos (\\frac{π}{6}) + \\cos x\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\sin x \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) + \\cos x \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x}{2} + \\frac{\\cos x}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x + \\cos x}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5197ab4-4e77-5da4-a06e-95284d6f010f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056870} {:answer/id #uuid "10934ea1-aaa6-5df7-9018-8a7d96895c9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056871} {:answer/id #uuid "435d6fcb-7928-5703-a3af-cd0fa64e1d1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056872} {:answer/id #uuid "5805d066-53f8-5759-ac95-75e64893aa70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #e